//
// PROBE: `and` and `or`, and the mathematical comparison spellings.
//
// `and` and `or` pull two values and convert each with `conv(BOOL)`, as `not`
// does, so an integer is false at zero
// (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/stdlib/logic/logic_ops_fun.rs:39-130). A
// string that is no boolean spelling panics the reference (F68), so this
// probe hands them none.
//
// `≠`, `⩾` and `⩽` alias `!=`, `>=` and `<=`
// (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/stdlib/create_aliases.rs:32-34), and
// reverse their operands as those do: `1 2 ⩽` asks whether 2 is at most 1.
//
"probe: and" println
true false and println
true true and println
1 0 and println
1 1 and println
"probe: or" println
true false or println
false false or println
0 0 or println
"probe: the mathematical spellings" println
1 2 ≠ println
1 1 ≠ println
1 2 ⩽ println
1 2 ⩾ println
